I dislike about sokoban that it is in one sense a 
stereotypical addition to a rogue-like: Make another
branch, find nice object(s) as reward and that's it.

Even worse, sokoban is Nethack-atypical in its 
non-randomness. I know the sokoban levels (that come 
with vanilla) from heart and it is so boring. Hence 
I've added some other ones (I think they're from Pasi 
Kallinen) but they are rather difficult compared to 
vanilla (until I know them from heart, too).

The best way to make sokoban again fun to play (applies
only to me, of course) would be randomization of levels.
Unfortunately, I don't have even the slightiest glimpse
about how to produce random sokoban puzzles.

OTOH I guess that sokoban has been introduced to help
unspoiled players because it makes life simpler at an
early point. This is a good thing, of course.


